[[00:16:25]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=985s) >> Staff report. >> Good afternoon, chairman, members of the finance committee. Uh my name is Robin Lman. I'm the city treasurer. Thank you for the opportunity to provide some additional information on the final reappropriation for last fiscal year.

[[00:16:38]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=998s) The memo I provided contains the full details, but I want to highlight the key points, particularly those affecting the

[[00:16:44]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1004s) general fund reserves and the self- insurance fund. The total reappropriation request is approximately $5 million. of that amount 1,631,979

[[00:17:00]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1020s) is being requested from general fund reserves. The remaining approximately

[[00:17:03]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1023s) 3.3 million is supported by additional revenue and reserves from our other funds. So those requests do not use

[[00:17:10]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1030s) general fund reserves. The majority of the general fund requests reflects the way we manage our budget throughout the year. As I have explained in the past, there are certain costs that are very difficult or impossible to accurately

[[00:17:23]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1043s) predict when we predict prepare the budget more than a year in advance. These include employee sick and vacation vac payouts for when an employee leaves

[[00:17:32]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1052s) the city, accident related costs,

[[00:17:34]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1054s) vandalism and theft, utilities, fleet

[[00:17:38]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1058s) fuel, parts and labor. Rather than

[[00:17:41]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1061s) overbudgeting these items in every department and tying up funds that may not be needed, we budget them based on the best information available and make necessary adjustments at year end. We

[[00:17:53]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1073s) also do not require departments to reduce their other operating expenditures to cover costs that they really have very little control over. For fiscal year 2026, we are requesting

[[00:18:03]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1083s) approximately 97,000 for accident and

[[00:18:06]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1086s) damage claims, 120,000 for natural gas and electricity

[[00:18:10]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1090s) increases, 142,000 for fleet cost

[[00:18:14]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1094s) increases, 172,000 for employee sick and vacation

[[00:18:18]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1098s) payouts, and approximately 36,000 for

[[00:18:21]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1101s) vandalism and theft expenses.

[[00:18:24]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1104s) There are also several larger, more specific general fund requests that I want to point out. We are requesting

[[00:18:30]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1110s) 149,000 for higher than anticipated

[[00:18:33]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1113s) inmate housing costs at the Larmy County Detention Center as well as an approximately 378,000 for the combined

[[00:18:41]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1121s) communication center. The communication

[[00:18:44]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1124s) center increase was primarily due to several previously hard to fill vacate vacant positions being filled during the year. We are also requesting approximately 155,000 for the municipal court and

[[00:18:56]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1136s) former senior center renovation design contract that was previously approved by the governing body and $350,000 for the

[[00:19:04]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1144s) purchase of the property at 803 West 16th Street which was previously approved by the governing body as well.

[[00:19:11]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1151s) I also want to provide some context on the self- insurance fund request because the $2.7 million reappropriation is a

[[00:19:18]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1158s) very large number. Since the city is

[[00:19:21]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1161s) self-insured, we essentially act as our

[[00:19:24]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1164s) own health insurance company. The premiums paid by the city and our employees go into this fund and we use those dollars to pay our employees health care claim expenses.

[[00:19:35]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1175s) Fiscal year 2026 was a particularly high

[[00:19:38]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1178s) claims year. Our benefit consultant has

[[00:19:41]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1181s) advised us that based on their experience, the self insurance, their self-funded plan can generally expect a more difficult claims year every five years. We've had our plan for four years now and we've had very good claims experience in fiscal years 23, 24, and 25. We also purchase stop-loss insurance to protect the city when claims become exceptionally high. It protects us both

[[00:20:06]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1206s) when an individual has extremely high medical expenses and when the city's claims as a whole becomes exceptionally high. For the overall plan, the

[[00:20:15]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1215s) insurance begins paying when our claims reach 100% of an the established

[[00:20:21]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1221s) threshold. At the end of fiscal year 26, we were still below that threshold at 87%.

[[00:20:28]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1228s) The goal is 80% or lower, which is based

[[00:20:30]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1230s) on the Affordable Care Act's requirement that 80% of all premiums collected must

[[00:20:36]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1236s) go to pay for medical care and quality improvement rather than administration, overhead, and profit. It is also

[[00:20:42]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1242s) important to understand that the 2.7 million reappropriation does not represent a $2.7 million loss to the

[[00:20:50]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1250s) fund. We received approximately 12.2 2

[[00:20:53]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1253s) million in revenue during the year and had 12.9 million in expenses. So the

[[00:20:59]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1259s) self- insurance fund decreased approximately by 690,000 for the entire

[[00:21:04]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1264s) fiscal year. The fund ended June 30th

[[00:21:07]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1267s) with a reserve of approximately $3.7

[[00:21:10]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1270s) million. For context, when we began the self- insurance fund on July 1st of 2022, we

[[00:21:17]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1277s) started with approximately 1.4 million in reserves. As far as how much we

[[00:21:22]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1282s) should maintain in reserves, our benefits consultant has recommended a minimum of six months of claim expenses

[[00:21:29]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1289s) with 12 months being the ideal target.

[[00:21:32]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1292s) Looking at our claims experience over the four years we have been self-insured, we have averaged approximately 9.3 million in claims

[[00:21:40]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1300s) annually. Based on that average, 6

[[00:21:43]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1303s) months would be approximately 4.7 million and 12 months would be approximately 9.3 million. As I said, we

[[00:21:51]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1311s) ended fiscal year 26 with approximately 3.7 million, which represents just under

[[00:21:57]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1317s) five months of average claims expenses.

[[00:21:59]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1319s) So, our first goal is to maintain at that least at least at the six-month level and over time continue toward the

[[00:22:06]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1326s) longer term reserve level recommended by our benefits consultant. This is why we

[[00:22:11]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1331s) build reserves in the first place. They allow us to absorb a higher claims year like fiscal year 2026 without

[[00:22:18]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1338s) immediately having to make significant changes to employee benefits or contributions. In fact, that was the reason for establishing the reserve target when we first became self-insured. You may also recall

[[00:22:29]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AED7FDEZ-5k&t=1349s) through the fiscal year 27 budget process, the governing body approved a $1 million transfer from general fund

